# id  tag  kind  t_s  alt_km  L_si_W  flag  note
1 - first_light 0.0030 100.000 1.6299e+05 info  L_si first exceeds 1e-6 of its peak. This is just a visibility threshold; the real value depends on your sensor floor and on where the simulation starts (zstart).
2 A ablation_onset 1.4760 86.854 1.7401e+06 stylized  Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~87 km as low-confidence. Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin, volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
3 F flare 1.4985 86.654 1.9361e+06 stylized  Light rises x1.3 in 0.06 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: no breakup within 0.05 s (growth of existing pancakes). Dust groups supply 0% of the rise and 0% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
4 Y first_yield 4.8630 57.035 4.1259e+08 physical  Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 0.2 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5 / H_f in [R22]).
5 F flare 4.9380 56.381 1.0921e+09 stylized  Light rises x12.4 in 0.22 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 0 at 57.0 km (99% of m0); split gen 0 at 55.8 km (99% of m0). Dust groups supply 74% of the rise and 68% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
6 B first_breakup 5.0010 55.834 2.0890e+09 stylized  Spread factor reached f_split = 2: the body breaks into 4 children plus 20 % of its mass as dust. The dust has a large area-to-mass ratio, decelerates and ablates within a fraction of a second, which makes a sharp flare. The instantaneous release is a model simplification. Light grew x5.1 between first yield and this breakup (pancake spreading).
7 F flare 5.3230 53.055 7.1834e+09 stylized  Light rises x1.8 in 0.18 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: yield gen 1 at 53.7 km (38% of m0); split gen 1 at 52.5 km (37% of m0). Dust groups supply 38% of the rise and 53% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
8 F flare 5.7255 49.630 1.5489e+10 stylized  Light rises x1.6 in 0.13 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with: split gen 1 at 50.5 km (18% of m0); yield gen 2 at 50.1 km (13% of m0); yield gen 1 at 49.9 km (12% of m0) +3 more. Dust groups supply 6% of the rise and 32% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic cascade.
9 P peak 6.0385 47.047 2.1744e+10 physical  Maximum light. It sits ~+1.8 km from the peak of energy deposition (45.2 km) because the luminous efficiency tau(v) falls as the fragments slow (mass-weighted speed here 19.6 km/s).
10 b bump 6.0628 46.855 2.1304e+10 stylized  Small fluctuation, 11% above the local trend; coincides with a split (gen 2) at 46.7 km. The fine structure of this phase is set by the cascade rules, so its pattern is not predictive of a real event.
11 D rolloff 6.7303 41.974 7.9961e+09 physical  Light has fallen to 1/e of the peak 0.69 s after it. Cause: the kinetic energy is being used up (speed 72% of v0, 34% of the mass still in flight) and tau(v) drops with speed. Analogue of Phase 7 (decline until dark flight) in [R22].
12 - drag_overtakes_ablation 6.8882 41.021 5.0199e+09 stylized  Drag work now exceeds the kinetic energy carried off by ablated mass. The ratio ablation/drag is about Lambda v^2/(2 Q Cd), so this happens when the speed falls below ~14 km/s (from the model's heating law).
13 T tail 8.9530 32.609 2.1726e+07 low-confidence  Below 1e-3 of the peak the light is controlled by groups being retired when they slow below v_dark = 3.0 km/s and by the tau taper (2-4 km/s). Do not interpret structure below this level.
